. ********************************************************************
. **# Hyp 1
. ********************************************************************
. 
. ***Hyp 1:
. /* NULL HYPOTHESIS
> After controlling for sugar
> level, consumer choices, purchase likelihood, and WTP are driven primarily by flavor liking and perceived sweetness. 
> Magnesium information and higher magnesium content in the lab-produced
> beverage do not meaningfully change the probability that a participant 
> would choose the lab beverage over the competitor or the WTP for it.
> *********
> ALT HYPOTHESIS 
> Alternatively, we can state that magnesium functionality
> information and higher magnesium content increase the probability 
> that the lab-produced beverage is chosen and raise WTP and 
> purchase likelihood for it, while flavor liking and perceived sweetness remain
> important but not exclusively dominant drivers of choice.
> 
> *********
> What is this hypothesis asking...?
> Magnesiusm. WTP. Certainty. Flavor liking. Sweetness. Sugar, which might just 
> be sweetness....
> 
> 
> * I need to make a plan for the variables.
> I'm thinking that the cleanest way to do this is by breaking them into what each
> represents.
> From there, I'll go line by line and do what I need to do for each var
> Primarily I'll be genning, labeling, so that I can cleanly examine the stats
> for each
> */
. 
. 
. ********************************************************************************
. **# Start Defining 
. ********************************************************************************
. * First I need to make value lables that make sense according to the
. * CSV so that they can be plug and play and not have to define as I go
. 
. * gender
. * randomizer
. * 5 point importance scale
. * 5 point agreement scale
. * 3 point certainty scale
. * 5 point agreement scale
. * flavors
. * 5 point refreshing scale
. * 9 point hedonic scale
. * 0 to 4 intake frequency scale
. 
. 
. ************************************************************
. **## Value labels
. ************************************************************
. 
.         label define            gender_lbl 1 "Male" 2 "Female", replace
{txt}
{com}.         label define            day_lbl 1 "Day 1" 2 "Day 2", replace
{txt}
{com}.         label define            yesno_lbl 0 "No" 1 "Yes", replace
{txt}
{com}. 
.  
.         label define            randomizer_lbl ///
>                                                 1 "Randomizer 1" ///
>                                                 2 "Randomizer 2" ///
>                                                 3 "Randomizer 3" ///
>                                                 4 "Randomizer 4", replace
{txt}
{com}. 
. 
.         label define            imp5_lbl ///
>                                                 1 "Not at all important" ///
>                                                 2 "Slightly important" ///
>                                                 3 "Moderately important" ///
>                                                 4 "Very important" ///
>                                                 5 "Extremely important", replace
{txt}
{com}. 
. 
.         label define            sure3_lbl ///
>                                                 1 "Low certainty" ///
>                                                 2 "Moderate certainty" ///
>                                                 3 "High certainty", replace
{txt}
{com}.         
. 
.         label define            agree5_lbl ///
>                                                 1 "Strongly disagree" ///
>                                                 2 "Disagree" ///
>                                                 3 "Neither agree nor disagree" ///
>                                                 4 "Agree" ///
>                                                 5 "Strongly agree", replace
{txt}
{com}. 
.         label define            flavor2_lbl ///
>                                                 1 "Blueberry" ///
>                                                 2 "Berry blend" ///
>                                                 3 "Fruit Punch" ///
>                                                 4 "Grape" ///
>                                                 5 "Lemon Lime" ///
>                                                 6 "Orange" ///
>                                                 7 "Pineapple" ///
>                                                 8 "None of them" ///
>                                                 9 "Other", replace
{txt}
{com}. 
.         label define            hedonic9_lbl ///
>                                                 1 "Dislike extremely" ///
>                                                 2 "Dislike very much" ///
>                                                 3 "Dislike moderately" ///
>                                                 4 "Dislike slightly" ///
>                                                 5 "Neither like nor dislike" ///
>                                                 6 "Like slightly" ///
>                                                 7 "Like moderately" ///
>                                                 8 "Like very much" ///
>                                                 9 "Like extremely", replace
{txt}
{com}. 
. 
.         label define            refresh5_lbl ///
>                                                 1 "Not at all refreshing" ///
>                                                 2 "Slightly refreshing" ///
>                                                 3 "Moderately refreshing" ///
>                                                 4 "Very refreshing" ///
>                                                 5 "Extremely refreshing", replace
{txt}
{com}. 
. 
.         label define            intake5_lbl ///
>                                                 0 "Never" ///
>                                                 1 "Rarely" ///
>                                                 2 "Sometimes" ///
>                                                 3 "Often" ///
>                                                 4 "Very often", replace
{txt}
{com}. 
